You may need to rethink that strategy. At high levels wizards are pretty
much all powerful. But a lower levels, they don't have enough HP and
spells to be effective wizards, and not enough STR or CON to be effective
combat wombats. So you compromise by dressing like a CW and let your
familiar take on most of the riffraff. Go ahead and wear the banded or
mithril, the dwarven helm and shoes. mithril is better because it's 
lighter. 

All of my successful wizards (including my ascending one) lucked into
dragon scale early in the game. In the early game consider sacrificing
spellcasting for that better AC. Especially if you're going to do the
MPR, because after you get the AC points, you can generally ditch the
armor and still be somewhat negative.

